// Focused view: Federation Edge — inbound federation gateway.

views {
  style element.tag = #frontend   { color blue }
  style element.tag = #backend    { color sky }
  style element.tag = #data       { color secondary }
  style element.tag = #adminPlane { color indigo }
  style element.tag = #federation { color green }

  view serviceFederationEdge of velox.federationEdge {
    title "Services / Federation Edge"
    description '''
      Stateless inbound federation gateway. Terminates mutual TLS from peer instances,
      verifies the ed25519-signed envelope on every request, and routes the call to the
      internal service that owns the targeted MIMI endpoint. Holds no private keys, no
      durable storage, and no session state.

      Routing table (WIP — tracks draft-ietf-mimi-protocol):

      | Endpoint                                      | Routed to     | Notes |
      |-----------------------------------------------|---------------|-------|
      | `/keyMaterial/{user}`                         | Identity      | Subject to consent check |
      | `/identifierQuery/{domain}`                   | Identity      | Scoped by searchability policy |
      | `/requestConsent/{targetDomain}`              | Identity      | Records inbound consent request |
      | `/updateConsent/{requesterDomain}`            | Identity      | Records a consent decision |
      | `/update/{roomId}`                            | Delivery      | MLS commit / proposal ingest |
      | `/submitMessage/{roomId}`                     | Delivery      | Encrypted application message |
      | `/notify/{roomId}`                            | Delivery      | Inbound fanout from peer hub |
      | `/groupInfo/{roomId}`                         | API           | GroupInfo for external joins |
      | `/reportAbuse/{roomId}`                       | API           | Abuse report with franked message |
      | hub-coordination forward (peer assumed us hub)| Interconnect  | Handoff when role changed |

      After authenticating the call and routing to the owning service, verified Commits
      are republished directly to the local `messages` Kafka topic — there is no
      separate ingress topic.

      ---

      **mTLS (mutual TLS)** — MIMI-conformant channel authentication: both client and server
      certificates are validated per federated domain. Velox additionally requires the request
      body to carry an ed25519 signature over canonicalised content for hop-independent
      integrity even when a peer operator terminates TLS at a load balancer.

      **Routing-only** — Federation Edge is intentionally dumb. It does not implement MIMI
      semantics, does not touch Scylla, does not hold the ed25519 private key. Each internal
      service remains the authoritative owner of its endpoints.

      **Stateless** — Edge pods can be scaled horizontally behind an L4/L7 load balancer with
      no session affinity. Retries and idempotency are delegated to the owning service.

      **MIMI (WIP)** — draft-ietf-mimi-protocol. Endpoint names and wire formats (TLS
      presentation language) are not yet RFC-stable; the edge is expected to evolve.
      Until MIMI stabilises, Edge also accepts the legacy Velox-native federation envelope
      for backward compatibility with peers that have not adopted MIMI.
    '''
    include *
    include -> velox.federationEdge ->
    autoLayout LeftRight 120 80
    style otherVelox { color green }
  }
}
